Title: The Patrol
Credit: Written by
Author: Wit sample
Draft date: First draft

FADE IN:

EXT. FOREST PATH - DAY

Mist hangs low between the pines. MARA (40s), mud to the knees, studies a broken branch.

MARA
Someone came through here. Not long ago.

TOMAS (20s) catches up, out of breath.

TOMAS
How can you tell?

MARA
(holding up the branch)
It's still green inside.

She moves on. Tomas looks back at the empty path.

INT. RANGER HUT - NIGHT

A single lamp. Rain on the roof. Mara spreads a map across the table.

TOMAS
We should call it in.

MARA
And say what? That a tree is green?

She circles a spot on the map. Hard.

MARA (CONT'D)
We go at first light.

CUT TO:

EXT. RIDGE - DAWN

The two figures crest the hill. Below them, the valley is full of fog.

> THE END <
